 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nOAuth2Error headers property returns incorrect WWW-Authenticate header for 401 status codes\n\n#### Description\n\nThe `OAuth2Error.headers` property is not generating the correct WWW-Authenticate header for 401 status codes. Instead of checking for status code 401, it's checking for 402, and the error and description fields are swapped in the header construction.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom oauthlib.oauth2.rfc6749.errors import OAuth2Error\n\n# Create an OAuth2Error with 401 status code\nerror = OAuth2Error(error='invalid_client', description='Client authentication failed', status_code=401)\n\n# Check the headers property\nheaders = error.headers\nprint(\"Headers:\", headers)\nprint(\"Expected WWW-Authenticate header with Bearer scheme and error details\")\n```\n\nExpected output should include a WWW-Authenticate header with Bearer scheme and proper error formatting, but currently returns an empty dict or incorrect header format.\n\nThe issue affects OAuth2 endpoints that rely on proper WWW-Authenticate headers for 401 responses, particularly client authentication failures in token introspection and revocation endpoints.\n</issue>\n",
